WEBVTT

00:01.418 --> 00:03.128
At the very beginning,

00:03.545 --> 00:05.088
it was an orb.

00:09.760 --> 00:14.555
After receiving various stimuli,

00:14.556 --> 00:16.517
the Orb began to transform.

00:19.978 --> 00:22.231
He could take on any form

00:22.648 --> 00:26.193
and create any object.

00:36.912 --> 00:40.999
In his human form, he had a dream.

00:43.585 --> 00:47.214
And it was to enjoy a peaceful life.

02:16.053 --> 02:17.887
(To Your Eternity Season 3)

02:17.888 --> 02:21.975
(Episode 1 A Peaceful World)

02:23.936 --> 02:26.187
Cleaning time has started.

02:26.188 --> 02:30.317
Students, please go to your assigned areas
and remove the weeds.

02:31.360 --> 02:32.818
According to one theory,

02:32.819 --> 02:37.407
these roots come from the giant tree
of the ancient western capital, Renril.

02:37.741 --> 02:40.576
In order to destroy the darkness
that rules the world,

02:40.577 --> 02:44.622
the messenger of God, the sacred roots
of the tree, covered the entire world.

02:44.623 --> 02:46.833
And there it is,
the cleanup-time tradition:

02:46.834 --> 02:49.460
fun facts with the vice president
of the Occult Research Club.

02:49.461 --> 02:51.963
It's not the Occult Research Club.
It's the Creative Literature Club.

02:51.964 --> 02:53.130
Hanna.

02:53.131 --> 02:55.800
Aoki, clean up properly.

02:55.801 --> 02:56.717
Okay!

02:56.718 --> 02:58.302
But these roots

02:58.303 --> 03:01.556
keep growing every day.

03:01.557 --> 03:03.891
We pluck them and they grow again.

03:03.892 --> 03:06.894
Herbicides don't work either.

03:06.895 --> 03:08.479
Senpai, Tamaki.

03:08.480 --> 03:10.231
Let's make this the theme
for the October issue

03:10.232 --> 03:11.817
of the Occult Research Magazine.

03:12.401 --> 03:13.818
President, what do you think?

03:13.819 --> 03:15.612
We're the Creative Literature Club.

03:17.155 --> 03:18.698
That's amazing.

03:18.699 --> 03:22.119
These are from the competitions
Mizuha joined, right?

03:23.078 --> 03:23.912
Mizuha.

03:24.246 --> 03:25.496
Are you going home?

03:25.497 --> 03:26.790
Let's go home together.

03:27.416 --> 03:29.585
I have to go somewhere else.

03:31.211 --> 03:32.629
Rikuya, don't mind it.

03:33.672 --> 03:38.050
Yesterday, I returned Mizuha's hair tie
that she forgot to take.

03:38.051 --> 03:41.554
Then she smiled and said to me,
"Thank you."

03:41.555 --> 03:43.264
She even touched my hand.

03:43.265 --> 03:45.016
It was originally my hair tie.

03:45.017 --> 03:48.227
She said her birthday's coming up
and asked me for it.

03:48.228 --> 03:49.270
You look so happy.

03:49.271 --> 03:50.771
I'm glad I gave it to her then.

03:50.772 --> 03:51.856
Excuse me,

03:51.857 --> 03:54.400
when is Mizuha's birthday?

03:54.401 --> 03:55.861
April 6th.

03:56.486 --> 03:59.615
April 6th. Remember that.

04:00.365 --> 04:01.408
Okay!

04:03.410 --> 04:05.829
It feels so peaceful.

04:08.332 --> 04:10.667
The world I've been looking forward to

04:11.877 --> 04:13.629
is right here.

04:15.464 --> 04:17.423
Mizuha, what about the Naginata Club?

04:17.424 --> 04:18.467
I quit.

04:18.842 --> 04:19.926
Again?

04:19.927 --> 04:22.470
I got bored, so I quit.

04:22.471 --> 04:25.057
You've quit a few clubs before, right?

04:25.724 --> 04:27.975
Let's see, which ones did I quit?

04:27.976 --> 04:31.479
The Tennis Club, the Kendo Club, and...

04:31.480 --> 04:34.023
That's weird. None of them lasted long.

04:34.024 --> 04:37.568
I worked hard and got results,
but once I felt satisfied, I grew bored.

04:37.569 --> 04:39.862
I've got good results in every club.

04:39.863 --> 04:41.405
So don't you complain.

04:41.406 --> 04:44.576
Senpai's so cool! You're so strong.

04:45.077 --> 04:46.077
Vice President.

04:46.078 --> 04:49.330
For our Occult Research Magazine,
how should I write this part?

04:49.331 --> 04:52.625
"Even now, the messenger of God
extends his roots and continues to fight,

04:52.626 --> 04:54.710
longing for world peace."

04:54.711 --> 04:56.296
Just write it like that.

04:56.547 --> 04:58.507
What is peace?

04:58.924 --> 05:00.717
Does it mean no worries?

05:01.093 --> 05:03.720
Or is it freedom, and everyone is happy?

05:04.179 --> 05:06.807
Yes, I think that's how it should be.

05:07.224 --> 05:08.474
And one more thing...

05:08.475 --> 05:11.603
it's being in the same room
as the one you love.

05:12.646 --> 05:15.273
When all the darkness
in the world is gone,

05:15.274 --> 05:19.277
the messenger of God will be
resurrected with his 11 disciples.

05:19.278 --> 05:23.239
That's when the tree's roots
will stop growing,

05:23.240 --> 05:26.201
and peace will come to the world.

05:39.673 --> 05:41.967
What a beautiful world.

05:42.676 --> 05:46.096
How long has it been since I fell asleep?

05:48.265 --> 05:49.473
Let's confirm it.

05:49.474 --> 05:51.852
I have to see the world
where peace has come.

05:52.144 --> 05:55.647
That's right. I'm free now.

06:03.488 --> 06:05.573
Is that in the way?

06:05.574 --> 06:07.659
You can remove it if you want.

06:07.910 --> 06:11.913
If I remove it, the roots
I worked so hard to expand will...

06:11.914 --> 06:13.582
It'll be fine.

06:13.832 --> 06:14.957
Why?

06:14.958 --> 06:16.167
I'm not...

06:16.168 --> 06:19.296
It's true that you're not complete yet.

06:20.297 --> 06:26.219
But you've taken root on the surface
of the earth and wiped out the enemy.

06:26.220 --> 06:28.514
You deserve a reward for that.

06:31.808 --> 06:32.935
Reconnection.

06:37.648 --> 06:41.652
I gave you the ability
to reconnect even when cut off.

06:42.069 --> 06:43.361
Well then, Fushi,

06:43.362 --> 06:44.905
we will meet again.

06:45.364 --> 06:46.531
You did well.

06:46.532 --> 06:49.910
Enjoy your own life from now on.

06:53.497 --> 06:55.666
Reconnection?

06:56.291 --> 06:58.877
The ability to reconnect
even when cut off?

07:05.259 --> 07:06.717
That's amazing!

07:06.718 --> 07:08.177
What's with that guy?

07:08.178 --> 07:11.139
Why didn't he give me
such a great ability sooner?

07:13.267 --> 07:14.101
Let's go.

07:14.977 --> 07:16.436
To the new world!

07:36.331 --> 07:37.206
Someone got hit!

07:37.207 --> 07:39.083
Call an ambulance!

07:39.084 --> 07:40.127
What?

07:49.511 --> 07:50.928
It's so hard.

07:50.929 --> 07:52.930
Where's the horse that's pulling this?

07:52.931 --> 07:54.474
How does it move?

07:55.809 --> 07:57.895
Are you okay?

07:58.353 --> 07:59.854
It might hurt later.

07:59.855 --> 08:01.398
I'll take you to the hospital. Get in.

08:02.482 --> 08:03.400
In that?

08:13.535 --> 08:15.453
Are you a foreigner?

08:15.454 --> 08:17.205
Forget it. I'll pay for you.

08:17.206 --> 08:19.373
Can I post a video of you online?

08:19.374 --> 08:20.751
Sure. Thank you.

08:32.554 --> 08:33.514
I'm so happy.

08:34.264 --> 08:35.557
I'm over the moon.

08:36.308 --> 08:38.060
This is so much fun.

08:44.149 --> 08:45.775
This drink is delicious!

08:45.776 --> 08:47.444
What kind of egg is in this?

08:48.111 --> 08:51.615
I think everyone will like this world too.

08:53.242 --> 08:55.536
Sorry to keep you waiting.

09:15.097 --> 09:16.807
Fu-chan!

09:17.307 --> 09:19.309
Where am I?

09:21.478 --> 09:22.478
Help me!

09:22.479 --> 09:24.273
March is all alone now...

09:27.568 --> 09:28.777
Mr. Hollow.

09:31.400 --> 09:33.406
Fu-chan!

09:33.407 --> 09:36.159
(Yanome Historical and Cultural Museum)
Fu-chan!

09:37.494 --> 09:39.912
Cleaning time is over.

09:39.913 --> 09:42.416
Thank you for your hard work, students.

09:45.586 --> 09:46.961
What are you guys doing?

09:46.962 --> 09:49.590
The roots have stopped growing.

09:50.465 --> 09:52.717
I've been keeping track since I was six.

09:52.718 --> 09:55.721
These roots grow
an average of one meter a day.

09:56.388 --> 09:58.599
This means true peace has arrived.

09:59.016 --> 10:01.434
Now's the time to uncover
the truth of the legend.

10:01.435 --> 10:04.646
President, tomorrow is Saturday.
Let's have an outdoor activity.

10:05.147 --> 10:07.982
Let's check
where these roots are coming from.

10:07.983 --> 10:11.319
I'm not going. It's not like I'm
in the Occult Research Club.

10:11.320 --> 10:14.239
I want to go. Can I?

10:15.490 --> 10:16.408
Of course!

10:16.867 --> 10:19.578
But don't you have classes on Saturdays?

10:19.995 --> 10:22.789
I can take a day off.

10:29.046 --> 10:30.255
Mizuha.

10:30.923 --> 10:31.964
Grandpa.

10:31.965 --> 10:35.844
How are you? You've grown so much.

10:36.345 --> 10:38.722
Grandpa, long time no see.
Why are you here?

10:39.097 --> 10:40.223
Mom...

10:40.224 --> 10:41.600
Let's go inside.

10:42.059 --> 10:43.227
Mom...

10:46.063 --> 10:47.898
Mom.

10:49.650 --> 10:51.400
Tomorrow's Saturday. Can I go out?

10:51.401 --> 10:52.902
Mizuha, did you know?

10:52.903 --> 10:54.695
Yuu-chan from the 15th floor

10:54.696 --> 10:57.448
is attending a ballet competition in Hena.

10:57.449 --> 10:59.367
So, do you want to learn ballet too?

10:59.368 --> 11:03.162
I won the grand prize
in that competition when I was ten.

11:03.163 --> 11:04.997
Huh? Really?

11:04.998 --> 11:06.374
Mom, look at this.

11:06.375 --> 11:08.501
I passed last month's test.

11:08.502 --> 11:09.919
So tomorrow...

11:09.920 --> 11:12.172
That's my girl. You're so outstanding.

11:13.090 --> 11:14.465
I already quit the Naginata Club.

11:14.466 --> 11:17.802
- Let me take a day off...
- Why? You can't give up so easily.

11:17.803 --> 11:20.429
But I won first place
in the competition a while ago...

11:20.430 --> 11:22.807
I'm so proud of my daughter.

11:22.808 --> 11:25.101
Why don't you learn to play an instrument?

11:25.102 --> 11:28.521
Maybe the flute...
or the piano in the storeroom.

11:28.522 --> 11:30.524
I've learned all of that.

11:31.108 --> 11:33.025
I see.

11:33.026 --> 11:34.695
Mom, I think...

11:35.654 --> 11:39.867
I'll take a break
from learning new things.

11:46.915 --> 11:49.083
No. I'll keep doing my best.

11:49.084 --> 11:50.001
I see.

11:50.002 --> 11:53.505
Then think about
what you want to win next time.

12:10.522 --> 12:12.065
I want to die.

12:15.736 --> 12:16.945
So itchy...

12:22.743 --> 12:24.952
Mizuha isn't here.

12:24.953 --> 12:27.747
Maybe something urgent came up.

12:27.748 --> 12:29.415
Didn't she contact you, President?

12:29.416 --> 12:31.919
Neither of us has a phone.

12:34.588 --> 12:36.380
Just as I thought.

12:36.381 --> 12:37.715
These roots cross the sea

12:37.716 --> 12:40.635
and extend all the way
to the west of Renril.

12:40.636 --> 12:43.514
I'm one step closer
to proving my hypothesis.

12:45.849 --> 12:47.934
Is that so? That's great!

12:47.935 --> 12:49.519
All right, that's all for today.

12:49.520 --> 12:50.436
Thank you, guys.

12:50.437 --> 12:52.856
No! We're going fishing now.

12:56.860 --> 12:58.402
Ninannah.

12:58.403 --> 13:01.031
This place has changed a lot.

13:01.740 --> 13:04.743
I think March's footsteps
are coming from around here.

13:05.536 --> 13:10.207
I have to go and pick up March
before she gets lonely and starts crying.

13:12.459 --> 13:14.335
She'll like this drink.

13:14.336 --> 13:16.505
Drinking it will make her happy.

13:17.089 --> 13:17.922
March!

13:17.923 --> 13:19.258
It's me. I'm here to pick you up...

13:37.317 --> 13:38.902
Who's out there?

13:42.698 --> 13:46.367
March... seems to belong in that house.

13:46.368 --> 13:47.369
I can't disturb her.

13:47.995 --> 13:50.580
Where does everyone belong?

13:50.581 --> 13:52.040
What would make them happy?

13:52.916 --> 13:55.418
What should I do? Where should I go?

13:55.419 --> 13:57.212
Where does this river flow to?

13:57.671 --> 14:00.840
Why are some rocks sharp
while others are round?

14:00.841 --> 14:03.009
I like small rocks.

14:03.010 --> 14:04.761
The bubble tea is good.

14:05.345 --> 14:06.722
What am I to them?

14:07.097 --> 14:10.684
If I stay in the water,
will everyone forget me?

14:11.101 --> 14:13.228
Don't you think it doesn't match?

14:13.937 --> 14:15.439
I'm talking about the fish.

14:15.856 --> 14:17.690
I don't think it belongs
in such a dirty bucket.

14:17.691 --> 14:20.152
There must be a better place for it.

14:20.569 --> 14:21.527
I'm sorry.

14:21.528 --> 14:23.655
I'll bring a new bucket next time.

14:25.407 --> 14:27.491
Aoki, it's time for me to go home.

14:27.492 --> 14:28.910
Me too.

14:28.911 --> 14:30.454
I'm leaving too.

14:30.954 --> 14:33.290
Okay. See you on Monday.

14:43.550 --> 14:45.886
No, I have to do something.

14:46.303 --> 14:49.389
Grain by grain, the sand is clear,
and so are my thoughts.

14:51.808 --> 14:55.646
I think I've created something incredible.

14:57.397 --> 15:00.067
Hey, look. I did a great job, didn't I?

15:19.044 --> 15:20.504
I caught it!

15:33.600 --> 15:35.978
(To Your Eternity Season 3)

15:38.689 --> 15:40.858
I'm sorry, but please forget about this.

15:42.734 --> 15:44.652
You... You just transformed.

15:44.653 --> 15:46.079
No, you appeared from thin air.

15:46.080 --> 15:47.905
Teleportation? Alien?

15:47.906 --> 15:50.784
Lizardman? Merman?

15:51.201 --> 15:52.703
You're the messenger of God!

15:53.787 --> 15:54.871
Wait a minute!

15:54.872 --> 15:57.915
I'm Yuki Aoki, vice president
of the Occult Research Club.

15:57.916 --> 15:59.500
We publish a monthly magazine.

15:59.501 --> 16:01.503
Please let me interview you!

16:05.007 --> 16:06.425
What are you doing?!

16:07.009 --> 16:10.095
Have you never seen a camera before?

16:12.973 --> 16:15.475
What do you say? Want to come to my place?

16:16.310 --> 16:18.352
Let's start by chatting.

16:18.353 --> 16:20.271
I won't do anything bad to you.

16:20.272 --> 16:21.814
I know you're scared.

16:21.815 --> 16:24.108
But I promise I won't
do anything bad to you.

16:24.109 --> 16:25.985
If you don't like it, you can leave.

16:25.986 --> 16:28.155
Just for a while.

16:30.449 --> 16:31.533
Wait!

17:01.438 --> 17:03.065
You're amazing.

17:03.565 --> 17:06.777
You can turn into anything.

17:07.903 --> 17:10.531
But I can't become anyone.

17:12.449 --> 17:14.326
Where are you going?

17:14.993 --> 17:16.078
Where to...

17:20.582 --> 17:22.875
I-I can go anywhere, right?

17:22.876 --> 17:23.919
See you.

17:26.547 --> 17:28.215
I can't stand up.

17:29.258 --> 17:31.133
You're not hurt.

17:31.134 --> 17:32.469
I can't walk anymore.

17:32.886 --> 17:34.930
Take me home.

17:38.058 --> 17:39.935
I guess I have no choice.

17:40.811 --> 17:43.437
Brother, what's wrong?

17:43.438 --> 17:44.857
Who are you?

17:47.609 --> 17:49.402
I'm leaving then.

17:49.403 --> 17:52.030
Wait! You'd better explain this clearly.

17:53.073 --> 17:55.658
Some fish and some transformation thing?

17:55.659 --> 17:58.035
Why is Yuki in so much pain?

17:58.036 --> 18:01.163
He's just pretending to be in pain.

18:01.164 --> 18:03.165
I'll call the police.

18:03.166 --> 18:06.544
I don't know what the "police" is.
Do whatever you want.

18:06.545 --> 18:07.628
Don't go!

18:07.629 --> 18:08.921
Grandpa, you've got it all wrong.

18:08.922 --> 18:11.174
He's the one who saved me.

18:11.175 --> 18:12.551
What did you say?

18:14.303 --> 18:16.180
He... He transformed!

18:17.931 --> 18:20.058
So fluffy!

18:20.475 --> 18:22.727
See? This is his power.

18:22.728 --> 18:25.814
Grandpa, let's keep it. Please?

18:27.691 --> 18:30.067
I don't know what you can eat.

18:30.068 --> 18:32.196
I removed the green onions for you.

18:43.540 --> 18:45.583
You can stay here tonight.

18:45.584 --> 18:48.795
No, you can stay here forever.

18:51.465 --> 18:54.635
Well... if you insist.

18:55.135 --> 18:57.513
I'll stay here.

18:59.598 --> 19:01.516
There, there.

19:01.517 --> 19:04.477
Good boy, you're so cute!

19:04.478 --> 19:06.479
What's your name?

19:06.480 --> 19:07.396
Fushi.

19:07.397 --> 19:09.190
Fushi, nice to meet you.

19:09.191 --> 19:10.983
Remember my name too.

19:10.984 --> 19:12.318
I'm Yuki Aoki.

19:12.319 --> 19:13.862
Yuki Aoki.

19:14.238 --> 19:16.030
I'm Aiko.

19:16.031 --> 19:18.450
- Aiko.
- I'm Kazumitsu.

19:18.867 --> 19:19.952
Kazumitsu.

19:20.452 --> 19:21.453
Love it!

19:25.165 --> 19:27.708
Oh, right. I have a favor to ask.

19:27.709 --> 19:28.751
What is it?

19:28.752 --> 19:31.796
Actually, I have other companions.

19:31.797 --> 19:33.590
Can I bring them here?

19:34.007 --> 19:35.174
Companions?

19:35.175 --> 19:36.510
Grandpa, it's okay, right?

19:36.885 --> 19:39.512
We still have empty rooms.

19:39.513 --> 19:41.765
You can bring them here anytime.

19:46.770 --> 19:48.020
A horse!

19:48.021 --> 19:49.272
A girl and a horse
popped out of his hands!

19:49.273 --> 19:50.773
Oh my gosh!

19:50.774 --> 19:52.316
She's a cat.

19:52.317 --> 19:54.027
The horse is the horse.

19:54.403 --> 19:55.612
Doesn't it have a name?

19:56.196 --> 19:57.864
It's been a while, you two.

19:57.865 --> 19:59.575
I'll be in your care from now on too.

20:02.578 --> 20:03.911
Yuki, thank you.

20:03.912 --> 20:06.122
But are you sure about this?

20:06.123 --> 20:08.916
A friend's friend is still a friend.

20:08.917 --> 20:10.585
It's as simple as that.

20:10.586 --> 20:12.253
A friend...

20:12.254 --> 20:13.796
Yuki, Aiko.

20:13.797 --> 20:16.632
You mustn't tell anyone
about Fushi and his companions.

20:16.633 --> 20:18.968
Only the three of us live in this house.

20:18.969 --> 20:19.887
Got it?

20:20.053 --> 20:20.887
Of course.

20:20.888 --> 20:23.514
If the government
or the Space Development Bureau finds out,

20:23.515 --> 20:25.892
they could be taken away by force.

20:25.893 --> 20:28.311
We can't hand them over
to animal protection groups

20:28.312 --> 20:29.646
or child counseling centers.

20:30.105 --> 20:32.356
This is our secret.

20:32.357 --> 20:34.026
I'll keep my mouth shut.

20:34.484 --> 20:35.651
Listen, everyone!

20:35.652 --> 20:38.197
I found Beast Boy!

20:38.947 --> 20:41.365
On Saturday, I caught a pufferfish.

20:41.366 --> 20:42.783
Then it suddenly turned into a person.

20:42.784 --> 20:44.452
In that instant,
I thought he was from the future.

20:44.453 --> 20:46.162
Then he turned into an octopus and a mole.

20:46.163 --> 20:48.331
So I thought he must be Beast Boy.

20:48.332 --> 20:50.041
And Beast Boy turned out to be

20:50.042 --> 20:53.002
an alchemist's dog-type
all-purpose weapon.

20:53.003 --> 20:55.463
- What is he talking about?
- Beats me.

20:55.464 --> 20:56.672
Yuki.

20:56.673 --> 21:00.301
Didn't I tell you not to try black magic
because it destroys your mind?

21:00.302 --> 21:02.303
Come to my house if you don't believe me.

21:02.304 --> 21:04.972
Beast Boy is very fluffy now.

21:04.973 --> 21:05.932
Fluffy?

21:05.933 --> 21:06.849
Do you want to see it?

21:06.850 --> 21:08.936
I remember you like fluffy things.

21:09.353 --> 21:10.561
Mizuha!

21:10.562 --> 21:12.063
I'm sorry I couldn't make it on Saturday.

21:12.064 --> 21:15.651
But I've temporarily joined
the Creative Literature Club.

21:16.401 --> 21:18.778
Do you want to come too, Mizuha?

21:18.779 --> 21:21.073
It's a really cute dog,
all covered in fur.

21:21.490 --> 21:23.324
Let's have fugu hot pot at my place too,

21:23.325 --> 21:24.951
with some crab and squid.

21:24.952 --> 21:26.745
Sorry, I have class.

21:28.038 --> 21:32.291
Will your family accept
that Beast Boy you said?

21:32.292 --> 21:34.043
Of course, he's family.

21:34.044 --> 21:36.588
My grandpa and sister love Fushi.

21:37.297 --> 21:38.507
Fushi...

21:38.924 --> 21:40.842
That's the name of Beast Boy.

21:40.843 --> 21:41.802
You've heard of him?

21:42.344 --> 21:43.219
No.

21:43.220 --> 21:44.971
I just feel nostalgic.

21:44.972 --> 21:45.888
What?

21:45.889 --> 21:49.434
I remember there was a story
where this name once appeared.

21:50.894 --> 21:54.815
Yuki, your family is so kind.

21:55.190 --> 21:57.442
Mizuha, it's time for sports day practice.

21:58.777 --> 22:00.821
Our class is going to practice too.

22:04.491 --> 22:07.368
I'm so tired. My glasses are falling off.

22:07.369 --> 22:08.871
Wear contact lenses instead.

22:10.247 --> 22:11.707
Mizuha's going to participate
in the relay race.

22:18.213 --> 22:19.714
Mizuha, I'm sorry.

22:19.715 --> 22:20.965
Are you all right?

22:20.966 --> 22:22.341
Class Health Monitor, come here.

22:22.342 --> 22:24.303
Let's go to the infirmary.

22:25.637 --> 22:27.139
You sprained your ankle, right?

22:27.681 --> 22:29.099
Don't force yourself to stand up.

22:32.936 --> 22:35.688
Why are you crying?

22:35.689 --> 22:36.607
Because...

22:45.991 --> 22:47.534
It hurts, doesn't it?

22:48.577 --> 22:50.787
Don't neglect your injury.

24:29.970 --> 24:31.971
(Next Episode Preview)

24:31.972 --> 24:34.349
Encounters in a new world,

24:34.766 --> 24:38.979
reunions with companions from the past,

24:39.813 --> 24:42.690
and in a world full of thrills,

24:42.691 --> 24:45.527
what will they bring to Fushi?

24:46.361 --> 24:48.113
The journey of the immortal

24:48.906 --> 24:50.908
begins again.

24:51.992 --> 24:54.995
(Episode 2 A Knot in My Heart)
